#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/Design.tsx
msgid "design.unsaid.2"
msgstr "Later I felt that was too fine a grain, and too much of an imposition. As long as the treatment follows generally accepted accounting principles, the rest is for me to judge, and to write down the reasons. The teacher knows about this project and will keep an eye on the content; if there is a different view, it can simply be changed. Every choice of this kind is made a setting you can switch, not a rule written in stone."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/Design.tsx
msgid "design.statements.title"
msgstr "Reading the statements backwards"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/Design.tsx
msgid "design.layout.3"
msgstr "I do not want to take sides; I only want to put the differences where they can be seen."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/Design.tsx
msgid "design.layout.2"
msgstr "What I have done is put the two side by side: the statements are shown in the course layout, with a mark beside the items that do not exist in the current International Financial Reporting Standards, and you can open each one to see what is done today. In the lab you can also switch the whole set over to the standards version and see, for the same transactions, where the numbers differ under the two sets of rules."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/pages/Design.tsx
msgid "design.play.2"
msgstr "I would like it to feel more like a walk, where a wrong turn means you simply go back and try again, rather than an exam to race through. The stars only record where you have been."

